quran[30]{c,v,t}:
  87,16,"But you (deniers) prefer the life of this world,"
  87,17,while the Hereafter is far better and more lasting.
  87,18,"This is indeed (mentioned) in the earlier scriptures,"
  87,19,the scriptures of Ibrahim (Abraham) and Musa (Moses).
  88,1,Has the news of the overwhelming calamity reached you?
  88,2,"Some faces on that Day will be humiliated,"
  88,3,overstressed (and) exhausted.
  88,4,"They will burn in a Blazing Fire,"
  88,5,(and) made to drink from a boiling spring.
  88,6,"They will have no food except a bitter, thorny shrub,"
  88,7,neither nourishing (them) nor availing (them) against hunger.
  88,8,"Some faces on that Day will be glowing blissfully,"
  88,9,well pleased with their (righteous) endeavour.
  88,10,"(They will be) in a magnificent Paradise,"
  88,11,where they will not hear any vain talk.
  88,12,"In it, there is a flowing spring,"
  88,13,"(and) in it, there are raised couches,"
  88,14,"and goblets (decently) set in place,"
  88,15,"and silken cushions laid in rows,"
  88,16,and splendid carpets spread out.
  88,17,"Do they not reflect on the camels, how (remarkably) they have been created?"
  88,18,"And the sky, how it has been raised high?"
  88,19,"And the mountains, how they have been firmly set?"
  88,20,"And the earth, how it has been levelled out?"
  88,21,"So (continue to) remind (them), for your duty is only to remind."
  88,22,You are not (appointed as) a watcher over them (to compel them).
  88,23,"But whoever turns away and disbelieves,"
  88,24,Allah will inflict upon him the greatest punishment.
  88,25,"Indeed, to Us will be their return,"
  88,26,"then, indeed, upon Us will be their Reckoning."
